From b3f5e671499fd457e24516706f5c3c8ebb6f5984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Apr 2024 03:33:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 834/960] downstream: iommufd/viommu: Add IOMMU_VIOMMU_ALLOC
 ioctl

Add a new ioctl for user space to do a vIOMMU allocation. It must be based
on a nesting parent HWPT, so take its refcount.

IOMMU driver wanting to support vIOMMUs must define its IOMMU_VIOMMU_TYPE_
in the uAPI header and implement a viommu_alloc op in its iommu_ops.

Reviewed-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Kevin Tian <kevin.tian@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Kunkun Jiang <jiangkunkun@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Yihua Jin <jinyihua@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Li Wei <liwei818@huawei.com>
